# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings, on every platform (ledger #1205).
#
# `ikigai-devtools`' vector-drift compares shared vectors by their raw bytes, and the
# tic-tac-toe template language's normative cases live in `crates/tic-tac-toe/README.md`,
# copied verbatim into the polyglot faces. A Windows clone with `core.autocrlf=true` would
# otherwise check that README out with CRLF, and the copy would read as drift. The index is
# already LF throughout (`git ls-files --eol`, 2026-10-10), so this needs no renormalize.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
